  "notes": "Pure WebGL demo (three.js, GPU-instanced): realistic satellite Earth with atmospheric rim glow and day/night shading floats in a nebula starfield; thousands of dashed great-circle flight arcs in neon magenta/yellow/green/cyan cluster at the limb, with diamond/SVG plane markers. The only UI chrome is the stock dark dat.GUI panel (collapsed to an 'Open Controls' bar in the capture) with coloured left-edge stripes per control type, a GitHub credit link bottom-left and a monospace lat/lng readout bottom-right. Globe appears to auto-rotate (lng readout changed between loads). Drag/zoom camera controls could not be verified, so mapNav is not coded."
